INSERT INTO `site_pages` (`id`, `slug`, `page_kind`, `title`, `summary`, `body`, `meta_title`, `meta_description`, `is_published`, `published_at`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(1, 'refund-policy', 'refund_policy', 'Refund Policy', 'When a Moonji order can be refunded, and how to ask.', '<h2>Moonji Refund Policy</h2>\n<p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> 8 September 2026<br><strong>Effective Date:</strong> 8 September 2026</p>\n<p>Moonji sells symbolic, creative digital placements. Every package is delivered as a shareable link within minutes of a successful payment, together with a printable PDF certificate. This policy explains when a refund is available.</p>\n\n<h3>1. What you are buying</h3>\n<p>You are buying a digital experience: a message placed at coordinates on our Moon scene, for the duration of the package you chose. This does not grant ownership, property, naming rights, or any legal interest in the Moon or any celestial body.</p>\n\n<h3>2. Delivery</h3>\n<p>Delivery is complete when the shareable link (and, for Archive, the QR card) is issued after payment clears. That usually happens within a few minutes. If payment succeeds but the link is not issued, contact us and we will either complete delivery or refund the charge.</p>\n\n<h3>3. When we refund</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Payment was taken but the message was not placed, or the share link never arrived, because of a fault on our side.</li>\n<li>You were charged twice for the same order.</li>\n<li>A charge was made in error (wrong amount, or a payment you did not authorise).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>4. When we do not refund</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>You changed your mind after the message was placed. A unique digital placement cannot be “returned”.</li>\n<li>You dislike the wording, photo, or voice clip you yourself submitted.</li>\n<li>The package duration has simply run out (Spark, Glow, Beacon and Archive expire on the dates shown at checkout).</li>\n<li>The Moon scene looks different on another device or browser — that is display, not a failed delivery.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>5. How to ask</h3>\n<p>Write to the support address on our Contact page with your order reference (the Moonji ID on your certificate) and a short description of the problem. We aim to reply within two working days. Approved refunds go back to the original payment method.</p>\n\n<h3>6. Chargebacks</h3>\n<p>If you open a dispute with your card issuer before contacting us, we may pause the message while the dispute is open. Please try us first — most delivery faults can be fixed the same day.</p>', 'Refund Policy · Moonji', 'Refunds for Moonji digital placements — when we refund, when we do not, and how to ask.', 1, '2026-09-30 14:44:00', '2026-09-30 14:44:00', '2026-09-30 14:44:00');
